cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its findings, please cite it as below."
title: "DriveGuard: geometric features beat CNNs for driver drowsiness detection"
abstract: >-
  A real-time driver drowsiness and distraction detector. Three hand-crafted
  eye and mouth aspect-ratio features over a 1.2-second causal window, fed to
  a linear SVM, reach 95.0% leave-one-person-out accuracy and outperform five
  CNN variants trained on identical frames under identical folds. A zero-shot
  object detector covers phone use, which facial geometry cannot represent.
  The work also reports a negative result: detectors trained on public
  drowsiness datasets learn head pose as a shortcut and score an F1 of 0.000
  on the drowsy class when transferred to independent footage.
type: software
